WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.569
Speaker 1: Given the attention right now on
the Nashville school shooting and on my comments

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:12.450
in response and on the hate mob that has been
sent at me by don jr and Candace Owens and

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.450
others.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.189
I am again going to take the opportunity to
talk about what doesn't work to reduce gun

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:21.019
violence and mass shootings and what does.

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:30.359
Now I want to contextualize this by reminding
you that you have very sort of pathetic solutions

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:35.280
from the right, which they don't even actually
believe in, which we know because they don't

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.280
fund them.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.280
I'll give you an example.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.600
They say say mass shootings are really about
mental health.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.140
Well, mental health might well be a component,
but if you believe that you should fund mental

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.050
health treatment services, which they do not.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.320
And in fact, in many states, every time there's
a proposal to increase funding for exactly

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.450
those types of services, they are against
funding it.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.450
They don't want to do it.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.890
We see the problems mental health, but we
won't do anything about it.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.750
Of course, the ubiquitous and ever present
thoughts and prayers before thoughts and prayers

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.000
and after thoughts and prayers and thoughts
and prayers and thoughts and prayers and the

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.510
thoughts and prayers do nothing.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.630
The thoughts and prayers do nothing.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:20.280
If prayer is important to you in difficult
situations, then by all means do it.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.130
But it is not policy to reduce gun violence.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:32.880
More recently now, they are targeting trans
people, drag shows, gender affirming care

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.540
because of the trans identity of the shooter
in Nashville, Tennessee.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.420
Give me a break.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.490
Give me a break now.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:46.710
If we could somehow pass legislation, if we
miraculously had the ability to get but build

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:53.880
consensus and actually pass some gun safety
legislation, what would I do?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.720
Such that we would make an impact?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.070
I am going to give you the disclaimer upfront
that I always do know.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:07.180
One of the bullet points I'm about to list
would prevent every mass shooting.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:12.490
We have 340 million people in this country
and every combination of mass shooting.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.129
No one rule would prevent every mass shooting.

00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:21.160
But taken together, these ten policies would
significantly reduce the number of mass shootings.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.040
Number one, end the gun show loophole.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:30.120
The gun show loophole is the fact that federal
law doesn't require unlicensed private sellers

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.989
to perform background checks on gun purchasers.

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:37.819
You go and you buy a gun at a dealer and they
do the background check.

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:38.819
Great.

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:43.540
Now, if you make a private sale, you as an
individual with no license to sell firearms,

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:49.170
if you make a private sale to someone else,
you are not required by federal law to have

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.260
that buyer background checks.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:55.250
Some states require it, but there is no federal
law and as a result, many states don't require

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.250
it.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.250
Would it solve every shooting?

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.080
No, but that is just obvious.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.240
That should be done.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.830
Number two, universal background checks.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:09.489
It would require almost all firearms transactions
in the United States to go through the end

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.709
ISIS National Instant Criminal Background
Check System.

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:17.710
This is also part of closing the private sale
exemption.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.940
So you've got the gun show loophole and the
private sale exemption.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.200
Both are about getting around background checks.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:31.170
At least 22 states and D.C. require background
checks for private sales, but they are not

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.140
required by federal law.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:38.330
Number three, mandatory waiting period from
when you go in and say, I'd like a gun, please.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.790
And when you get the gun.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.580
It won't prevent every shooting.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.370
Some people, some shooters have guns that
they've had for years.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.489
But for those who are going and saying, I
want to do a shooting, let me go and get the

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:52.750
gun, and you get it that day.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.530
For some of them, a mandatory waiting period.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.849
Maybe it's five days, maybe it's ten days.

00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:03.220
Might actually allow cooler heads to prevail
and might reduce the number of these shootings.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:07.160
Number four, no high capacity weapons for
those under age 25.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.390
But, David, they could get a handgun.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.819
Yes, they could.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:15.510
But in many of these incidents, not all, but
in many of these incidents with a handgun

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:22.260
rather than an AR 15, the number dead would
be lower and fewer people dying is better.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.169
I'd rather zero, but fewer is better.

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:30.949
Number five, mandatory gun insurance, which
is significantly more expensive without a

00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:33.270
parent cosigning.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:39.210
If you were under 25, this is both a financial
disincentive, which might just make the entire

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.280
thing more expensive, particularly for those
under 25.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:49.009
Remember, when we look at mass shooters overwhelmingly
under age 25, if you don't have a parent saying,

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:54.630
yeah, I think this makes sense and we're going
to get the insurance, it is dramatically more

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:55.920
expensive.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.729
Number six, if you're under 25 and you want
to get a gun, you should be required to provide

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:02.930
one, maybe two community support letters.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:08.880
These would be letters from adults who know
you, not your parents, who say, I am fine

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.150
with this individual having these firearms.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:13.360
I have no issues with that.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.710
And if there are issues, it doesn't mean any
random person in the community can say no

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.710
guns.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.509
But it would require more scrutiny.

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:26.990
And maybe if someone goes and tries to get
a gun and a teacher and whoever else says,

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:32.539
I have concerns about this individual, or
if they're not even able to find such individuals,

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:35.110
then maybe that person shouldn't be able to
get guns.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.970
Number seven, some weapons should be banned.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:43.060
There are simply there are some weapons that
are simply of no recreational or any other

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.190
value other than as mass killing machines.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:50.770
I'm not pretending I have the exact list right
here in front of me.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:53.750
People will disagree about what should be
on the list.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:58.310
Most people think the shoulder mounted RPGs
should be not allowed.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.050
Most people believe the handguns should be
allowed.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.620
Well, now we're now we're negotiating.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.000
Now we have to find what is the point.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.389
There are some weapons that should be banned.

00:06:07.389 --> 00:06:11.530
Number eight, there should be a periodic mental
health evaluation.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:15.110
There should be a mental health evaluation
at the beginning and there should be a mental

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.410
health evaluation periodically.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.870
Oh, but, David, that'll be expensive.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:23.690
Well, it should be paid by the licensing fees,
which maybe are too low.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:24.970
That's another issue to discuss.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:27.880
But there should be a periodic mental health
evaluation.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:32.759
You might be fine to have a gun at 25 and
then at 30 things have changed.

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:37.259
And if you were subjected to a mental health
eval, a mental health professional might say,

00:06:37.259 --> 00:06:39.600
you really shouldn't have this gun.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.979
Number nine, the licensing process should
be more extensive.

00:06:43.979 --> 00:06:47.800
You need a written and a practical test for
a driver's license.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.150
At minimum, it should be the same for guns.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:53.479
The training and licensing period shouldn't
be one weekend.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.610
It should be longer.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:07:01.050
More like with cars where there are hours
of driver's ed and practical.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.050
Why not?

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:06.389
Well, because the right wing gun lobby has
prevented it from being that way.

00:07:06.389 --> 00:07:10.259
And then number ten, there should be a gun
buyback program.

00:07:10.259 --> 00:07:15.449
Give people an off ramp that feels better
than supposed gun confiscation.

00:07:15.449 --> 00:07:20.639
No, one of these things will stop Every specific
shooter.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:24.430
Someone will write in and say, David, but
number nine wouldn't have stopped the Uvalde

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.729
D shooting.

00:07:25.729 --> 00:07:34.509
The point here is we would stop some of the
shootings and we would be able to then say,

00:07:34.509 --> 00:07:36.400
Look at the improvement.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:37.400
Where can we tweak?

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.889
Where can we do more?

00:07:38.889 --> 00:07:41.319
We have a Second Amendment.

00:07:41.319 --> 00:07:45.199
None of these affect that, but we could be
doing so much more.

00:07:45.199 --> 00:07:47.590
But none of this stuff will happen.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:50.630
With the current Republican Party and the
NRA.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:56.300
As powerful as it is also amazing, mental
health isn't an issue.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:01.979
No, the reason I want the mental health evaluations
is because I'm agreeing a factor is mental

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:03.050
health.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.669
There is also the cultural issue.

00:08:05.669 --> 00:08:13.530
The United States is unique and many Americans
don't understand how weird it is to see firearms

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:19.120
fetishized violence celebrated, intelligence
condemned.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:25.590
We need a cultural change where people stop
seeing firearms as the solutions to personal

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:26.819
or social problems.

00:08:26.819 --> 00:08:29.690
I don't know how in hell we do that.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.300
That's a big issue.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:38.390
In the meantime, though, ten policies, all
of which would prevent some mass shootings.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.700
So the thoughts and prayers don't work.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.400
I stand by that.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.150
Here's ten ideas that might.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.150
And you know what?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.340
What do we have to lose?

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.180
We're not fixing it.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.790
We've done nothing.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.970
And it hasn't solved the problem.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.259
Maybe it's time to try something new.

